1
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:03,992
Picture someone browsing a fashion store online.

2
00:00:03,992 --> 00:00:07,965
They find a dress, a jacket, or a linen shirt they love.

3
00:00:07,965 --> 00:00:09,176
The photographs look

4
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:10,252
beautiful.

5
00:00:10,252 --> 00:00:12,272
But one question remains.

6
00:00:12,272 --> 00:00:14,856
What could this actually look like on me?

7
00:00:14,856 --> 00:00:21,324
GRINDCTRL's AI Virtual Try-On brings that moment closer to a personal
shopping experience.

8
00:00:21,324 --> 00:00:25,568
On a supported Shopify product page, the shopper selects an item.

9
00:00:25,568 --> 00:00:27,746
Taps try it on with AI.

10
00:00:27,746 --> 00:00:29,216
and uploads a photo.

11
00:00:31,216 --> 00:00:36,440
The system generates a visual preview of that shopper wearing the selected
garment.

12
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:39,099
It's important to understand what this means.

13
00:00:39,099 --> 00:00:42,178
The preview helps someone explore a style.

14
00:00:42,178 --> 00:00:45,511
It isn't an exact measurement, a fit guarantee.

15
00:00:45,511 --> 00:00:48,538
or a replacement for real product information.

16
00:00:50,538 --> 00:00:52,886
Now the shopper has another question.

17
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:55,007
Does the shirt run oversized?

18
00:00:55,007 --> 00:00:56,456
Is there a size guide?

19
00:00:56,456 --> 00:00:58,353
What is the delivery policy?

20
00:00:58,353 --> 00:01:02,125
This is where Store Chat enters the same shopping journey.

21
00:01:02,125 --> 00:01:05,827
Instead of leaving the product page and searching across the website,

22
00:01:05,827 --> 00:01:08,222
The shopper opens the store assistant.

23
00:01:08,222 --> 00:01:13,654
Store Chat answers in English or Arabic using the information the merchant
has supplied.

24
00:01:13,654 --> 00:01:16,218
Accurate answers come from store knowledge.

25
00:01:16,218 --> 00:01:19,037
not from made-up stock levels or promises.

26
00:01:19,037 --> 00:01:20,657
If human help is needed,

27
00:01:20,657 --> 00:01:23,013
the AI hands off with a reason.

28
00:01:23,013 --> 00:01:26,247
The team picks up the conversation in a shared inbox.

29
00:01:26,247 --> 00:01:27,167
Assigns it.

30
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:28,527
adds a private note.

31
00:01:28,527 --> 00:01:30,559
and replies in context.

32
00:01:32,559 --> 00:01:35,152
Where appropriately configured and verified.

33
00:01:35,152 --> 00:01:39,209
Read-only order information can also support relevant questions.

34
00:01:39,209 --> 00:01:42,779
But the assistant shouldn't change orders. Promise refunds...

35
00:01:42,779 --> 00:01:46,638
or imply an integration exists when it hasn't been enabled.

36
00:01:46,638 --> 00:01:48,684
Let's connect the experience.

37
00:01:48,684 --> 00:01:50,491
A shopper sees a garment.

38
00:01:50,491 --> 00:01:52,434
previews it on their own photo.

39
00:01:52,434 --> 00:01:55,465
asks about the size and gets a helpful answer.

40
00:01:55,465 --> 00:01:57,340
If the question needs judgment,

41
00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:01,165
a real person continues from the conversation already started.

42
00:02:01,165 --> 00:02:02,545
for a fashion brand.

43
00:02:02,545 --> 00:02:05,134
The two tools belong to one journey.

44
00:02:05,134 --> 00:02:08,250
Virtual Try-On helps people picture the product.

45
00:02:08,250 --> 00:02:10,590
Store Chat helps them understand it.

46
00:02:10,590 --> 00:02:13,974
The merchant's team stays in control when it matters.

47
00:02:13,974 --> 00:02:16,250
See the live product experience.

48
00:02:16,250 --> 00:02:21,839
Explore the demo and discover how GRINDCTRL can fit your Shopify fashion
store.

49
00:02:21,839 --> 00:02:23,109
GRINDCTRL.

50
00:02:23,109 --> 00:02:24,706
Let shoppers see it.

51
00:02:24,706 --> 00:02:26,000
Let them ask.
